  "slug": "event-inquiry-incident-report-form",
  "title": "Event Inquiry Incident Report Form",
  "subtitle": "Record a booking-process failure in the inquiry pipeline, contain the client impact, and route correction and remediation to the responsible manager.",
  "description": "An original incident record for failures in the inquiry and booking process, such as a double-sold hold, a released hold, a missed response window, a misquoted rate, or a lost accessibility request. It captures incident identity, the factual account and contributing factors, client impact and containment, qualified review, corrective actions, and verified closeout.",
  "use_case": "Use when something in the inquiry-to-booking process went wrong and a client commitment, a date, or a record is affected. A coordinator records the facts and containment, and the responsible manager reviews the incident and approves corrective action. The report closes only after corrective actions are verified as effective and any residual risk is accepted in writing.",
  "risk_tier": "B",
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "incident_identity",
      "title": "Incident identity and routing",
      "guidance": "Bind the incident to the affected inquiry, order, and client.",
